# Context Persistence

- Keep a short project context file at `documentation/agent_context.md`.
- Read `documentation/agent_context.md` before resuming multi-step work when it is relevant.
- Update `documentation/agent_context.md` after meaningful progress, architectural decisions, debugging discoveries, or changes to the next-step plan.
- Include only durable context:
  - current implementation status
  - important decisions and trade-offs
  - known blockers and debugging facts
  - next recommended steps
- Never store secrets, passwords, tokens, private URLs with credentials, or copied sensitive config values in the context file.
- Keep the file concise and practical so the next session can continue work quickly.
